<title>SWITZERLAND: Nestle says no plan sell L'Oreal.</title>
<headline>Nestle says no plan sell L'Oreal.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Helmut Maucher, chairman and chief executive of Nestle SA, said the company had no intention of selling its stake in French cosmetics company L'Oreal or sell its Alcon pharmaceuticals division.</p>
<p>Maucher told a news conference he hoped Nestle could one day have a majority in L'Oreal. Nestle now has a 49 percent stake.</p>
<p>Industry analysts have often pondered the possibility of Nestle divesting itself of these two activities.</p>
<p>Commenting on Alcon, Maucher said: &quot;It is a succesful business and we don't see any reason to sell.&quot;</p>
<p>-- Zurich Editorial +41 1 631 7340</p>
</text>
